# expected: "Duplicate type 'Empty'"
#-
  Two bodies for one type name is a duplicate even when both are empty. This
  used to compile: duplicate detection asked whether the field list was still
  empty, which cannot distinguish "not defined yet" from "defined with no
  fields", so an empty redeclaration slipped through. The registry now records
  definedness directly.
-#
